    "resolutions": {
      "llms-txt-directive-html": "No agent-facing directive pointing to llms.txt was detected in the HTML of any tested page. Add a visually-hidden element near the top of each page (e.g., a div with CSS clip-rect) containing a link to your llms.txt. If your site serves markdown versions of pages, mention that in the directive too so agents know to request it.",
      "llms-txt-directive-md": "No llms.txt directive was detected in the markdown of any tested page. Add a blockquote near the top of each markdown page (e.g., \"> For the complete documentation index, see [llms.txt](/llms.txt)\").",
      "content-negotiation": "Your server ignores Accept: text/markdown and returns HTML. Some agents (Claude Code, Cursor, OpenCode) request markdown this way. Configure your server to honor content negotiation.",
      "markdown-link-portability": "1 of 1 markdown pages link in a way that depends on the base URL (root-relative links on 1). Emit absolute URLs when generating markdown: the canonical host is known at build time, so absolute links cost nothing to produce. Root-relative links resolve only while the fetch URL is still around, and agent pipelines lose it routinely, to summarization, to RAG chunking, or to content being pasted somewhere else."
